    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1075">

                <pb facs="0914" n="798" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg798"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/447.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Guadalajara to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Guadalajara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-20T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 20, 1912—11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> (Received April 21, 1912—11.30 a.m.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>State and War Departments’ promptness in shipping arms almost nullified by the
                    failure Minister for Foreign Affairs to send permits to admit them. Am still
                    uninformed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Magill.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
